      "description": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Symlink Attack when logs are written to a default directory that is widely writable. An unprivileged attacker can overwrite sensitive files by predicting a privileged process's log file path and pre-creating a symbolic link to this file, which the logging process will then follow and overwrite.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This is only exploitable if the attacker has access to the filesystem of the target machine and has permissions to create files (or symlinks) in the writable directory.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `github.com/golang/glog` to version 1.2.4 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/golang/glog/pull/74/commits/b8741656e406e66d6992bc2c9575e460ecaa0ec2)\n- [GitHub PR](https://github.com/golang/glog/pull/74)\n- [Google Groups Forum](https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/H-Q4ouHWyKs)\n- [Vulnerability Report](https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2025-3372)\n",
